cz:CN37 a impacto:eu-gdpr-DPIANotRequiredProcess ;
    skos:definition "A process which does not require a DPIA according to the Data Protection Authorities of the Czech Republic and which involves: Processing (processing operations) carried out by a person authorised to provide healthcare services who is not in an employment relationship. This person uses the necessary personal data only to provide healthcare services to the data subject (see recital 91 of the Regulation), and there is no systematic transfer to third countries, no processor is used for some processing operations on personal data of patients, or there is no sharing/linking of personal data of patients of two or more individual doctors."@en ;
    dpv:hasEntity impacto:dpv-EmploymentRelationship ;
    dpv:hasEntity impacto:dpv-NotEmploymentRelationship ;
    dpv:hasEntity impacto:dpv-SelfEmployedHealthcarePractitioner ;
